{
  // Type-checks the TESTS as well as src. The main tsconfig.json is `"include": ["src"]` because it
  // is the BUILD config — it emits to dist/ and must not compile tests into the artifact — so for
  // the life of this repo NO test file was ever type-checked at all.
  //
  // That is not cosmetic. `AnonPolicy.categories` is a Record<AnonCategory, boolean>, so adding a
  // category makes every object literal that omits it a type error. That is the tripwire meant to
  // stop a new detector from being silently OFF in the tests that claim to cover it. With tests
  // unchecked the tripwire never fired: CARD, PHONE and NATID were missing from four `categories`
  // literals, so those three detectors were quietly disabled in every screenshot-redaction and
  // anonymization test on this branch. Two of this plan's own defects reached review that way.
  //
  // Run it: `npm run typecheck`. `npm run build` is unchanged and still emits src only.
  //
  // WHAT THIS CATCHES TODAY: every file under src/ and scripts/, and 370 of the repo's 430 test
  // files — every test file not named in `exclude` below. That includes the whole anonymizer
  // surface this branch touches: anonymize, anonControl, anonEntities, anonDiscovered,
  // anonPipeline, imageRedact, ocrRedact, redactedExport, presidio, presidioPipeline,
  // presidioPending and presidioRoutes. A NEW test file is checked automatically, because the
  // include is the whole `tests` tree and only the named legacy files are skipped — which is the
  // point: the next AnonPolicy field addition cannot silently go missing in a test.
  //
  // WHAT IT DOES NOT CATCH: the 60 test files (plus one script) listed in `exclude`. Two of them
  // are in the PII area and are therefore the first ones worth reclaiming —
  // tests/server/presidioBroadcastCoverage.test.ts (7 errors, all "stub AIProvider is missing
  // `model`") and tests/analysis/ocrPipeline.test.ts. The rest carry a PRE-EXISTING backlog of
  // ~360 type errors that accumulated over the years tests went unchecked — missing `model` on
  // stub AIProviders, incomplete Finding/IocEnrichment literals, `as` casts between structurally
  // unrelated types, implicit `any` parameters. None of them currently causes a false pass, and
  // burning them down is deliberately NOT part of this change; the list is a debt register meant
  // to shrink. Deleting a line from it and making that file compile is the whole follow-up.
  //
  // It also does not catch anything OUTSIDE the type system: a test asserting the wrong thing, or
  // a category that is present in a literal but set to `false`, still passes. This closes the
  // "silently missing field" hole, not "the test is wrong".
  //
  // The list is exclusions BY FILE, not by rule, on purpose: a blanket loosening of `strict` would
  // have let the AnonPolicy omission through everywhere, which is the failure this exists to stop.
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    // No emit, and no rootDir constraint — `tests` lives outside the build's rootDir and this
    // config exists purely to check types.
    "noEmit": true,
    "rootDir": "."
  },
  "include": ["src", "tests", "scripts"],
  "exclude": [
    "scripts/ocr-redact-demo.ts",
    // Arrived from master (#238, command palette) in the merge that brought in the settings-save
    // fix — i.e. it is NOT part of this branch's work, and it is the newest entry on this list
    // rather than part of the historical backlog. It fails for one root cause with seven
    // knock-on effects: it imports `public/js/command-palette.js`, which has no declaration file
    // (TS7016), so every callback parameter derived from that import is an implicit `any`
    // (TS7006 x7). Reclaiming it means adding a `.d.ts` for that module — or enabling `allowJs`
    // for `public/js` — and belongs to whoever owns the command palette, not to this PR.
    // Worth noting the exclusion is proof the tripwire works: this file was checked
    // automatically the moment it landed, exactly as the comment above promises.
    "tests/analysis/commandPalette.test.ts",
    "tests/analysis/achHypotheses.test.ts",
    "tests/analysis/artifactBundleStore.test.ts",
    "tests/analysis/askGraphRag.test.ts",
    "tests/analysis/attackMitigations.test.ts",
